# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# The style is this file, not prose: `clang-format` settles it, and CI
# checks it (see the `format` job in .github/workflows/ci.yml).
#
# Base: Google, at 80 columns — which is what the code written before this
# file already was, so adopting it reformats nothing. (Issue #5 floated
# LLVM at 100; that would have churned every existing file to no benefit,
# and 80 keeps a side-by-side diff readable, which matters for a codebase
# whose diffs get read against hardware documentation.)
#
# clang-format is pinned in .llvm-version, because formatters disagree
# across major versions and a gate that depends on which one you happen to
# have installed is not a gate. CONTRIBUTING.md has the install line.
#
# C++ only. CMake files and shell scripts are reviewed by eye and, for the
# scripts, by shellcheck; JSON is left alone so CMakePresets.json can keep
# the blank lines that make it readable.

Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: Google
ColumnLimit: 80

# Comments carry most of the reasoning in this codebase, and they are
# hand-wrapped to sit well under the limit. Reflowing them would rewrite
# paragraphs the author shaped deliberately; the column limit still
# applies to them, it is just not enforced by re-breaking prose.
ReflowComments: false
